BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to Wheel Throwing with Naomi and Jack  — Sebastopol Center
  For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260730T000000
DTEND:20260731T000000
UID:8ac04b87ea2469e7ea2e2440322681ac@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Intro to Wheel Throwing with Naomi & Jack\n\n  \n    \n      \
 n        \n          $245.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nThursdays\, Ju
 ly 30th to August 27th\, 2:00-5:00pm (5 weeks) $200+ $45 Clay Fee (max 8 s
 tudents)This course is designed for students who are new to the potter’s
  wheel and eager to discover the fundamentals of wheel throwing. With an e
 mphasis on core technique\, each session builds a solid foundation in the 
 essential skills of centering\, opening\, pulling up walls\, trimming and 
 glazing — the building blocks that every potter returns to again and aga
 in.Each class begins with a demonstration focused on one or more of these 
 foundational techniques\, giving students a clear picture of the process b
 efore getting their hands in the clay. From there\, students work at their
  own wheels with plenty of time to practice\, explore and develop their fe
 el for the material. The goal is for each person to leave the course being
  able to make a thrown piece — a bowl\, a mug\, a vase — that is genui
 nely their own\, shaped by their emerging skills and their personal sense 
 of what they love about pottery.With two teachers in the room\, there is a
 mple opportunity for individual attention and hands-on guidance at every s
 tage of the process. At the same time\, there is real joy in learning alon
 gside others — watching a classmate pull up a wall for the first time\, 
 or seeing a finished glaze come out of the kiln — and that shared experi
 ence is very much a part of what makes this class special.No prior experie
 nce is necessary. All you need is curiosity and a willingness to get a lit
 tle muddy.About the Instructors: Naomi Fuchs brings a deep love of clay an
 d a genuine passion for sharing the experience with others to everything s
 he does in the clay room. She believes that each pot is an opportunity to 
 learn — about the nature of clay\, and about yourself. Naomi has been th
 rowing on the wheel for four years\, and in that time the practice has bec
 ome a grounding\, peaceful and creative part of her life that has deepened
  her connection to art and making. Her warm\, encouraging approach creates
  a space where beginners feel supported as they find their footing at the 
 wheel and begin to discover what clay can do in their hands.In just one ye
 ar\, pottery has become one of Jack Harrison’s passions—a craft that c
 ontinues to humble him\, calm him\, and inspire him as he shapes both the 
 clay and his own journey. Throwing vases is what he does most\, but he is 
 experienced in all areas of the wheel. Sharing his passion with others in 
 the studio has allowed him to become part of a community that supports and
  challenges each other. As a mellow\, focused individual\, beginners will 
 find comfort in learning from him.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n      
           Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/intro-to-wheel-throwing-with-
 naomi-and-jack
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
