SUMMARY:Jizo Peace Project  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Californi
 a
DTSTART:20260807T000000
DTEND:20260808T000000
UID:736f0807388ffa310a933f48c6c1b613@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering for Remembrance and Peace\,
  August\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $10.00\n        \n      \
 n    \n  \n\nFriday\, August 7\, 2026\; 1:30 – 4:00pmDue to limited capa
 city\, we are asking for a suggested donation of $10 to confirm your atten
 dance. Bring a copy of your receipt at check-in to Painting/Drawing Studio
  adjacent to Ceramics StudioJoin us for a monthly\, heart-centered gatheri
 ng where we come together to create Jizo guardians out of clay—symbols o
 f compassion\, protection\, and peace. Rooted in the Buddhist tradition an
 d echoed across many cultures\, Jizo figures traditionally honor children 
 and all who have passed\, those in transition\, and those in distress.This
  ongoing project is dedicated to remembering those lost to war\, with a sp
 ecial focus now on the approximately 19\,000 children who have perished in
  Israel and Gaza in recent years. Through the simple\, meditative act of w
 orking with clay\, we create benevolent beings that will become part of pu
 blic exhibits and peace sites\, offering spaces for reflection\, mourning\
 , and hope. Our gatherings conclude with a gentle ritual to honor the live
 s of these children.Located in the Painting & Drawing Room. The gathering 
 is open to ages 12 - adult\, and no prior clay experience is necessary—a
 ll clay and basic materials are supplied. Registration is required to part
 icipate.Donations are welcome to help cover materials and expenses. More t
 han a class\, this is a shared space of warmth and care—an opportunity t
 o tend to our own hearts while taking part in love in action.\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n         
